data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgrades to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which has several breaking changes:

### 1. `OpenApiAny` types removed (`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc.)
`Schema.Example` is now a `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode`:

```csharp
// Before
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

Add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;` and remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;`.

### 2. `OpenApiResponse` → responses are now referenced differently
`operation.Responses` changed from `OpenApiResponses` (a `Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>`) to `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` — this one likely still compiles, but if you hit issues it's because `OpenApiResponse.Description` is still valid. This part should work as-is.

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityScheme` / `OpenApiReference` changes
`ReferenceType` is now a string-based URI, and `OpenApiReference` no longer has a `Type` property with an enum:

```csharp
// Before
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference("#/components/securitySchemes/oauth2")
};
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
        { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    }
};
```

### 4. `Schema.Nullable` removed
Nullability is now expressed via the `Type` flags enum (`JsonSchemaType`):

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After — remove Null flag from Type
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

To **add** nullability: `property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type | JsonSchemaType.Null;`

---

### Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("#/components/securitySchemes/oauth2")
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```
